WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.850
For each attribute both systems write,
the check gives one of three results.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.200
A Finding when both update it: each overwrites
the other, and the command exits one.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.921
A Warn when one updates it and
the other sets it at creation:

4
00:00:13.921 --> 00:00:15.937
two sources for its first value.

5
00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:18.800
And Info when both set
it only at creation.

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.562
Two inputs need a reviewer.

7
00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:22.512
First, the alias list.

8
00:00:22.512 --> 00:00:27.412
SailPoint's field names are the
connector's, not necessarily Entra ID's.

9
00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:30.169
The check matches names
case-insensitively,

10
00:00:30.169 --> 00:00:32.926
and takes an alias for
each pair that differs.

11
00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:34.113
It doesn't guess.

12
00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:36.956
Which connector field writes
which Entra attribute

13
00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:39.412
is something to confirm
in the source's schema.

14
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:41.401
Second, the directory name.

15
00:00:41.401 --> 00:00:44.766
A wrong name would make every
attribute look unwritten,

16
00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:47.980
so the check refuses a name
the schema doesn't target.
